alsa mixer: map the volume linearly onto the mixer's range

MPD sets a hardware mixer on the scale that alsamixer shows, which follows the
mixer's dB values. On a USB DAC with a wide range that puts 50% at about -18 dB,
far louder than 50% of the DAC's own scale.

Streamer sets the DAC's volume from several sources, and for Bluetooth it already
uses the DAC's own scale (see the bluez-alsa patch). Do the same here, so that 40%
from a UPnP app is 40% of the mixer range, as "amixer set PCM 40%" would set it.

Upstream: not submitted; a change of behaviour that this project wants.

--- a/src/mixer/plugins/AlsaMixerPlugin.cxx
+++ b/src/mixer/plugins/AlsaMixerPlugin.cxx
@@ -112,8 +112,16 @@
 
 	[[gnu::pure]]
 	[[nodiscard]] double GetNormalizedVolume() const noexcept {
-		return get_normalized_playback_volume(elem,
-						      SND_MIXER_SCHN_FRONT_LEFT);
+		/* the position on the mixer's own scale, as "amixer" shows it */
+		long min = 0, max = 0, value = 0;
+		if (snd_mixer_selem_get_playback_volume_range(elem, &min, &max) < 0 ||
+		    max <= min ||
+		    snd_mixer_selem_get_playback_volume(elem,
+							SND_MIXER_SCHN_FRONT_LEFT,
+							&value) < 0)
+			return 0;
+
+		return double(value - min) / double(max - min);
 	}
 
 	[[gnu::pure]]
@@ -322,7 +330,12 @@
 {
 	assert(handle != nullptr);
 
-	int err = set_normalized_playback_volume(elem, 0.01*volume, 1);
+	/* the same position on the mixer's own scale: 40% is 40% of its range */
+	long min = 0, max = 0;
+	int err = snd_mixer_selem_get_playback_volume_range(elem, &min, &max);
+	if (err >= 0)
+		err = snd_mixer_selem_set_playback_volume_all(elem,
+							      min + lround(0.01 * volume * double(max - min)));
 	if (err < 0)
 		throw Alsa::MakeError(err, "failed to set ALSA volume");
 
